 "what_was_wrong_first": [
  "an add-only plan: `capability_planner` returned ['gzip','cp'] for a goal needing both, and running it failed because gzip consumed the file cp needed -- the plan was IMPOSSIBLE, not merely suboptimal, because the planner has no delete list",
  "the moved() subset as input: it drops `LOT: RETAINED` as 'unchanged', which deleted the precondition, so a rename was applicable to an empty world",
  "CARD alone as the state: `cp` and `touch` both raise the count by one and only one leaves a readable second name",
  "a delete subtracting BOTH READABLE and CONTENTS for one loss: `cp; rm` then reported zero readable names while the content sat readable in the copy",
  "a goal of {REMOVED>=1, READABLE>=1}: `rm` met it outright in a world holding a duplicate content, so no sequence was needed and the experiment proved nothing",
  "a goal of {REMOVED>=1, READABLE>=1, NAMES>=3}: still met by `rm` in a world already holding four names -- the same escape one world over",
  "two doors executed as recorded against DIFFERENT files: the census binds `cp` to in.json and `rm` to in.txt, so the sequence copied one file and deleted another and the content looked lost",
  "`len(after) < len(before)` as the removal test: a copy adds a name and a delete removes one, so a net count of zero hid a real removal",
  "a refusal control of 'three readable names', which is reachable by cp twice -- the planner rightly planned it and the control proved nothing"
 ],
